' Question: how does a Futures Grid keep an exchange-side stop under its position, and what does a restart do with it? (Planned: EPIC-039L)
' Explained by: ../06-runtime.md. Drawn by hand, high level.
@startuml 06-protective-stop
participant "Grid executor\n(bot's worker)" as G
participant "BotRunState /\nIBotStore" as S
participant "trading\n(IOrderSubmission)" as T
participant "exchange" as X

== after the opening fill, before the ladder is ready ==
G -> S : save record INTENDED\n(clientAlgoId, trigger price)
G -> T : place STOP_MARKET closePosition,\nMARK_PRICE
T -> X : POST algoOrder
X --> T : algoId, NEW
G -> S : save record STANDING
note over G : only now is the ladder declared ready

== a stop, in order: close first, cancel after flat ==
G -> T : reduce-only close (IExposureCloser)
G -> T : read position of the symbol
alt exchange position is zero
  G -> T : cancel the stop
  G -> S : record ENDED
else a read fails, or a close failed
  note over G : the stop stays standing
end

== the app was down ==
G -> T : read position and open algo orders
alt position, no stop
  G -> T : place the plan's stop; if it cannot stand,\nclose reduce-only
else flat, stop standing (orphan)
  G -> T : read again, then cancel the stop
else flat, stop TRIGGERED
  G -> S : STOPPED, protective_stop_triggered
end
@enduml
